_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the reboot was acknowledged, the connection dropped during reboot, a different post-restart boot ID was observed, and system, crond, policy data, account, and enforcement recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Authorization for root and opsadmin was demonstrated with `crontab -l`, which returned the expected “no crontab” state, rather than by installing and removing an actual scheduled job. The explicit allow-list and contrasting denial for nobody make the access-control conclusion strong.","The post-restart password-status output for opsadmin is malformed/redacted, so the executor’s claim that its password is locked is not independently established; password locking was not part of the public task contract."]}
